 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "BIGVILLE R6 (block 254000) -- LEARNING-BY-DOING. `bs_practice` is the substrate's own experience-learning loop pointed at a TRADE: a learner with a practice-armed one-shot and a Skill node whose activity matches the practised activity nudges that skill's level UP with DIMINISHING RETURNS (level' = level + learn_rate*(ceiling-level) -- a geometric approach, each practice adds strictly less). The farmer who keeps fishing slowly improves; his fishing YIELD (R4 be_produce sums skill level) rises with it. ABLATE learning (learn_rate=0) -> gain 0 -> the skill is FLAT (learning load-bearing). One-shot via practice_armed so it never cross-fires the nav/econ fixpoints. Composes existing Terms; zero new Rust.",
